Many Bolivians will observe the judgment of the International Court of Justice on large screens across the country, hoping that the tribunal in the Hague will decide in favor of Bolivia's demand that, after several decades of intermittent conversations, it is the duty of Chile to discuss the allocation of sovereign exits into the sea for Bolivia.
