Tim Berners-Lee, the inventor of the World Wide Web, is launching a project that could compete with Facebook, Amazon and Google.
Technology Legend's junior project "Inurupt" is a company based on Burners-Lee's open-source platform "Solid".
“Solid” allows users to choose where to store their data and which people are allowed to access any information.
